---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — Quackbit"
  description="Quackbit collects no data. Your habits live on your devices and sync through your own private iCloud."
>
  <main id="main" class="doc wrap">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 14 September 2026</p>

    <p>
      Quackbit is built to keep your information to yourself. There is no account, no sign-in,
      no advertising, and no analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. Quackbit does not collect, transmit, or sell any personal data. We do not run
      servers that receive your habits, and there is no third-party analytics or tracking SDK in
      the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
    <p>
      The habits you create and the progress you log are stored on your device. If iCloud is
      available and you leave sync on, that data is also stored in your <strong>private</strong>
      iCloud database (Apple CloudKit), tied to your Apple ID and governed by
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a>. We have no ability
      to read it.
    </p>

    <h2>Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      If you add a reminder, Quackbit asks for permission and schedules a local notification on
      your device. Reminders are scheduled and delivered by the system; no reminder data leaves
      your device for that purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>Widgets</h2>
    <p>
      The Home Screen and desktop widgets read the same on-device data as the app, through a
      shared container on your device.
    </p>

    <h2>Diagnostics</h2>
    <p>
      If you have opted in to share diagnostics with Apple, Apple may provide us aggregate,
      anonymized crash reports through App Store Connect. These are controlled by your device
      settings, not by Quackbit.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Quackbit is not directed at children and collects no data from anyone, including children.
    </p>

    <h2>Your control</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete any habit and its history inside the app. Deleting the app removes its local
      data; to remove synced copies, manage Quackbit's iCloud data in your device's settings or at
      <a href="https://www.icloud.com">icloud.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted here with a new date. Because the
      app collects no data, we do not expect meaningful changes.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy? Email
      <a href="mailto:info@quackbyte.dev">info@quackbyte.dev</a>, or visit our
      <a href={`${base}/support/`}>support page</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
